{"key":"e7743784d8831404","source_file":"Potts Ma - Me.json","source_id":19653,"source_url":"concordance-many-ppl-multus","term":"Many","headwords":["Many","Much"],"latin":["Multus"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Many","Much"],"latin":["Multus"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","AE","HH"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"2936","subsection":null},"text":"The middle of them = much.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"6172","subsection":"end"},"text":"Much, in the Word, is said of truths; great, of goods.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"6654","subsection":null},"text":"The people of the sons of Israel is many and numerous in comparison with us () = that the truths of the Church prevailed over the alienated scientifics... Many and numerous = to prevail; for to become many is predicated of truth.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"8712","subsection":null},"text":"Under Thousand, see this reference.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"8713","subsection":null},"text":"Under Hundred, see this reference.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"8714","subsection":null},"text":"Under Fifty, see this reference.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"8715","subsection":null},"text":"Under Ten, see this reference.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"9251","subsection":null},"text":"To be after many () = to be with many; thus to be consociated. AC 9252.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"HH","section":"349","subsection":null},"text":"They who have had much affection, receive much.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"336","subsection":"3"},"text":"Much, and multitude, are said of truths.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"337","subsection":"end"},"text":"There are two words which frequently occur in the Word; namely, great, and much; and great is predicated of good, and much (or many) of truths. AE 409:3.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"492","subsection":null},"text":"Many incenses () = truths in abundance. Explained.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"518","subsection":"36"},"text":"Many (waters) () is said from Falsity.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"521","subsection":null},"text":"Many men... () = all who were such.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"1033","subsection":null},"text":"Sitting upon many waters () = dominating over all things of the Word... Illustrated.","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"many","url":"/meta/potts/many/"}